From 36f10148b8fb219080f546da14c1f3f205b008fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:23:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): launchd plist names its job label so the
 gateway caps its stop drain [daveey]

launchd stamps XPC_SERVICE_NAME=<label> only on the job's main process. Since
the signed wrapper and the core-update launcher sit in front of stderr_timestamp,
every process below the wrapper reads XPC_SERVICE_NAME=0, so the gateway never
found its label, never read the live 60 s ExitTimeOut, drained a full 60 s and
launchd restarted into the still-draining gateway (start_refused
owner_alive=true, defect gateway-cc28b19bca; earlier fix t_01a18a872bab1aac only
kept the wrapper alive).

- generate_launchd_plist: HERMES_LAUNCHD_LABEL=<label> in EnvironmentVariables,
  inherited by every descendant.
- _load_launchd_exit_timeout: a darwin --external-supervisor gateway that still
  cannot read its budget assumes the gui-domain clamp (60 s, so the drain caps
  at 50 s) and writes exit-diag row gateway.launchd_budget_missing (warning).
- Test runs the real job chain (signed wrapper with XPC on the first process,
  XPC=0 below it, real stderr_timestamp) and asserts the leaf's
  launchd_job_label().
